  "body": "The standalone sdist checker accepted hidden PAX data, additional gzip archives, corrupt/truncated gzip framing and ambiguous generated identity metadata. This repair validates one bounded gzip stream through CRC/ISIZE/EOF, checks physical tar records and padding before logical parsing, rejects unrequired extensions, and validates singleton metadata identity.\n\n**Author verification completed; independent non-Author re-review required. Keep Draft.**\n\n| Identity | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Base | `review/adr0033-sdist-independent-20261023` |\n| Base HEAD / tree | `ef3ca118d4ab5e52dc2d1c7de384c3557509add2` / `ded7bd39fd86dd0d738404abf667beaf44fb06d0` |\n| Published HEAD / tree | `59307c40ea65554736e131cedd00f04c9906551b` / `5ea93707d62b542c84632515392ac6a35c36cd65` |\n| Final GitHub test merge | `e0c60765bd0d99b8276a8d0528dabfa7f4d6971a`, exact parents base + published HEAD, same effective tree |\n| Tested code commit / tree | `aaee34d31d2511cfec95d0bfa41a3a9733ac43e4` / `6552c028771f957a6e81c31b9f67b9016bf5b569` |\n\nThe second commit adds evidence only. Every executed source/test/script/workflow/lock input is byte-identical to the frozen tested code commit. The conservative acceptance hash changes with new unclassified evidence JSON/ZIPs: tested `508261ad3a6a2a95d55bbe5af95394f6db64fa9a0b2e823316b8853f81d3d1ec`; final `8413e49bbfd35224c6c864680809a8956a2eda4f1324b04c3247e792b32ebdaf`. No release-receipt transfer is claimed.\n\nAR-001/002/003 corrected; A-CI-01 documented and regression-tested. Existing 2 MiB compressed, 8 MiB regular-file and 512-member budgets stay unchanged. A separate whole-tar limit is 8,922,624 bytes. Actual Hatchling 1.32.4 needs no PAX keys, so the justified extension allowlist is empty.\n\nActual Author results, with overlapping counts:\n- All seven retained attacks now reject, including CLI exit 1/failed receipts. New regressions: **94 PASS**; old checker against the same cases: **72 FAIL / 22 PASS**.\n- Packaging: **151 PASS / 4 inherited FAIL**, exit 1.\n- Broad: **3,058 PASS / 59 FAIL / 20 ERROR**, exit 1. All 79 baseline nodes/phases/refusals/trace paths/functions match; **0 added, 0 resolved**.\n- CI planner/profile/execution/efficiency: **253 PASS**. Docs: **8 PASS**. Lint, format, SQLite policy and allowlisted placeholder docs build pass.\n- Installed I4/I5: **246 PASS per wheel**; I2/I3 pass. Original Access smoke fails on both, so installed orchestrator remains FAIL.\n- **3,531 / 5,888** unique ordinary nodes executed; **2,357 ordinary + one live + one benchmark** unexecuted. Full release acceptance was not run.\n\nNew measurements: **83,949,291 \u2192 677,902 bytes (99.19248633082559% reduction)**; 159 members, 5,921,698 regular-file bytes, 6,051,840 whole-tar bytes. All 159 direct/derived wheel members and RECORD rows match. All 155 product inputs and SQL/JSON/GraphQL resources remain. Separate fresh outside-checkout venvs verify CLI/schema/resources/DDL/integrity. Backend-only rebuild has no installed product or Git on PATH. Actual local Python 3.12.14 / SQLite 3.53.1; no SQLite setup/rebinding/matrix or guard relaxation.\n\nHosted evidence:\n- [Initial tests 39890829950](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/actions/runs/39890829950): PASS; actual sdist gate passed, 24 receipt payloads verified. Development runtime pytest 0.\n- [Initial Access 39890829878](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/actions/runs/39890829878): FAIL; broad **3,058/59/20** and original Access refusals preserved; 102 receipt payloads verified, distribution checks pass.\n- [Final tests 39892052621](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/actions/runs/39892052621): **development_checks_passed**, runtime pytest **0**, full_acceptance=false. All 21 receipt payloads, final feature/merge/tree and final acceptance hash verified. Receipt SHA-256 `3f799c38ad843d05b7fee4a57609ba124ad400e36e7447728aa0d62e2673e202`.\n- [Automatic final Access rerun 39892052634](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/actions/runs/39892052634): still running at handoff. This is a pending execution, not a PASS or independent acceptance.\n\n[Full Author report](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/59307c40ea65554736e131cedd00f04c9906551b/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0033-archive-hardening-20261023/REPORT.md), [196-payload evidence index](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/59307c40ea65554736e131cedd00f04c9906551b/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0033-archive-hardening-20261023/raw-evidence-index.json), and raw ZIP SHA-256 `610e484a214d7904dd318909bc57d2a8619423b1aca26a353711169349d6f2c2`.\n\nStartup live checks found no competing repair across 76 branches. Strictly stacked on #140; neither #139 nor #141/I6-A was integrated. Later integration of independent stacks requires separate effective-tree verification. Existing PRs/evidence/ADRs/product guards stay unchanged. No merge, release, deploy, real-catalog operation or automation modification.\n\nRemaining: final automatic Access execution, independent non-Author re-review, and inherited 79 product-stage failures/Access smoke. No action was denied or left pending approval; no push/PR outcome is uncertain.",
